{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaNa4WvDKja6kNsd5Cjt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I proved `myRev_append` in `Main.lean`, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem myRev_append (xs ys : List α) : myRev (xs ++ ys) = myRev ys ++ myRev xs := by\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => simp [myRev]\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [myRev, ih, List.append_assoc]\n```\n\nThe proof uses induction on `xs`:\n- **Empty list:** `myRev ([] ++ ys)` simplifies to `myRev ys`, which equals `myRev ys ++ []`.\n- **Non-empty list:** `myRev (x :: xs ++ ys)` unfolds to `myRev (xs ++ ys) ++ [x]`. The induction hypothesis rewrites that to `(myRev ys ++ myRev xs) ++ [x]`, and moving the brackets with `List.append_assoc` gives the goal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":8313,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":325,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8ad6f893-d513-460b-adac-7b347b594e0d","uuid":"5f2db7a9-a686-4bee-bee0-fd92504de16b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:12:23.799Z","request_id":"req_011CgaNa4G3LaEZGXmrpWwM3"}
